00:40:35,172 --> 00:40:41,172
Tropic Thunder is a 2008 satirical action comedy film directed by Ben Stiller,
who wrote the screenplay with Justin Theroux and Etan Cohen.

12
00:44:16,551 --> 00:44:22,551
The film stars Stiller, Jack Black, Robert Downey
Jr., Jay Baruchel, and Brandon T.

13
00:47:57,931 --> 00:48:03,931
Jackson as a group of prima donna actors making a Vietnam War film.

14
00:51:39,310 --> 00:51:45,310
When their frustrated director (Steve Coogan) drops them in the middle of a jungle, they are
forced to rely on their acting skills to survive the real action and danger.

15
00:55:20,689 --> 00:55:26,689
Tropic Thunder parodies many prestigious war films (specifically those based on
the Vietnam War), the Hollywood studio system, and method acting.

16
00:59:02,068 --> 00:59:08,068
The ensemble cast includes Nick Nolte, Danny McBride,
Matthew McConaughey, Bill Hader, and Tom Cruise.

17
01:02:43,448 --> 01:02:49,448
Stiller developed Tropic Thunder's premise during the production of Empire of the Sun in the
spring of 1987, and later enlisted Theroux and Cohen to complete a script.

18
01:06:24,827 --> 01:06:30,827
The film was greenlit in 2006 and produced by Stuart Cornfeld, Stiller, and Eric McLeod for DreamWorks Pictures and Red Hour
Productions as an international co-production between the United States, Germany, and the United Kingdom.

19
01:10:06,206 --> 01:10:12,206
Filming took place in 2007 on the Hawaiian island of Kauaʻi over thirteen weeks
and was the largest film production in the island's history.

20
01:13:47,586 --> 01:13:53,586
The extensive marketing campaign included faux websites for three of the main characters and their fictional films,
a fictional television special, and selling the energy drink advertised in the film, "Booty Sweat".

21
01:17:28,965 --> 01:17:34,965
Tropic Thunder was released in the United States on August 13, 2008.

22
01:21:10,344 --> 01:21:16,344
It received generally positive reviews for its characters, story,
faux trailers, and cast performances, with Downey Jr.

23
01:24:51,724 --> 01:24:57,724
being the most positively praised for his performance.

24
01:28:33,103 --> 01:28:39,103
However, the depiction of people with disabilities and the
use of blackface makeup attracted controversy.

25
01:32:14,482 --> 01:32:20,482
The film opened at the top of the American box office and retained the number-one position for three consecutive weeks,
ultimately grossing more than $195 million worldwide before its release on home media on November 18, 2008.

26
01:35:55,862 --> 01:36:01,862
Downey was nominated as Best Supporting Actor for an Academy Award, a BAFTA Award, a Screen Actors Guild Award, and
a Critics' Choice Movie Award, while both he and Cruise received nominations for a Golden Globe.

27
01:39:37,241 --> 01:39:43,241
The film explores themes of vietnam, movie business, satire, parody, jungle.

28
01:43:18,620 --> 01:43:24,620
The tone is lighthearted.
